# Return the frontier vertices of the global graph, scored and ranked the way
# Rrg::calculateGlobalPath ranks its candidates -- best first.

# If True, run one local sampling + gain evaluation pass first and merge its
# frontiers into the global graph, so the call stands on its own without
# auto_planning having ever run. Costs a full local RRG build (seconds), and
# resets the local graph, which the next planner iteration would rebuild
# anyway.
bool force_update
# If True, report the gains cached by the last planner iteration instead of
# re-evaluating them. Cheap, but frontiers grafted into the global graph since
# that iteration still carry a zero gain and will rank last for no reason.
bool skip_gain_refresh
---
std_msgs/Header header
bool success
# Sorted by exp_gain, descending.
planner_msgs/FrontierPoint[] frontiers
